course: dictionary
lesson: 2252
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Crash is a good example. You can use the words around it to find the right meaning.
explain: «Rules like "walk, don't run" exist so people don't crash into each other in corridors.» Here crash means to hit something hard. Try your meaning in the sentence: "so people don't hit each other hard in corridors" still makes sense, so this meaning fits.
explain: «A helmet that has had a hard crash should be replaced, even if it looks fine.» A bike helmet protects your head in a crash, so this crash is an accident. The word helmet is the clue.
fact: Crash can be a noun (a crash, crashes) or a verb (crash, crashes, crashed, crashing).
fact: A crash is an accident when a vehicle hits something hard.
fact: A crash can also be a sudden loud noise, like something falling or breaking.
fact: When a computer crashes, it suddenly stops working.
fact: Informally, to crash can mean to fall asleep very quickly because you are tired.
exercise: «A helmet that has had a hard crash should be replaced, even if it looks fine.» What does crash mean here? | A new kind of bike | A gentle bounce on a soft bed | To fly slowly over a lake | *An accident where something hits hard
exercise: My tablet keeps crashing when I open the game. What does crashing mean? | Winning the game with a big score | A loud roll of thunder in the sky | Going to sleep slowly on the sofa | *When a computer suddenly stops working
exercise: «The waves crashed on the rocks.» What does crashed mean? | Turned into ice in the cold | Moved quietly over the sand | Stopped to rest for a while | *Hit the rocks hard, with a loud noise
test: «A girl of eight in Canada rode in the front seat; in a small crash the airbag burst out with great force.» What is a crash in this sentence? | *An accident when a vehicle hits something | A soft, quiet place to sit | A fast swim in the sea | A kind of seatbelt
test: In «He will crash his bike into the wall», is crash a noun or a verb? | *Verb, it is an action | Adverb, it describes how | Noun, it is a thing | Pronoun, it takes the place of a name
exam: Which sentence uses crash as a sudden loud noise? | The car crash was on the news last night | My laptop crashed again during homework | I always crash out on the sofa after school | *The plates fell off the shelf with a crash
